{"id": "unknown-2026-05-11-002", "date": "2026-05-11", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 20, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Kenyan team explores Bangladesh SEZ, port development for cooperation", "content": "A Kenyan delegation recently concluded a five-day visit to Bangladesh aimed at strengthening strategic cooperation in the development and management of special economic zones and port infrastructure. \nThe visit focused on exchanging institutional knowledge, operational experiences and best practices to support industrial growth, logistics efficiency and investment promotion through bilateral cooperation. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/kenyan-team-explores-bangladesh-sez-port-development-for-cooperation-310218-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-11-003", "date": "2026-05-11", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 20, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh needs logistics upgradation to turn competitive: Think tank", "content": "Policy Exchange Bangladesh has called for urgent modernisation of the country’s port infrastructure, overhaul of trade facilitation systems, and activation of its dormant National Logistics Policy to stay globally competitive.  \nA 25-per cent cut in logistics costs could boost exports by 20 per cent, while cutting container dwell time by just a day at Chattogram would raise exports by 7.4 per cent, it said.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-needs-logistics-upgradation-to-turn-competitive-think-tank-310219-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-11-004", "date": "2026-05-11", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 20, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Maharashtra, Karnataka, Delhi, Haryana, TN host 85% of EU firms", "content": "While EU firms maintain a presence in every Indian state and union territory supporting 6 million jobs, Maharashtra, Karnataka, Delhi, Tamil Nadu and Haryana host 85 per cent of such firms, the economic footprint report released by the EU in India revealed. \nGujarat and Telangana are highlighted as the fastest emerging centres for new investment. \nManufacturing remains the primary driver (40 per cent). ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/maharashtra-karnataka-delhi-haryana-tn-host-85-of-eu-firms-310222-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-11-005", "date": "2026-05-11", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 20, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh gas crisis drives orders to Ludhiana", "content": "North India’s 30/1 combed yarn jumped from ₹338/kg to ₹348/kg in a single day (May 4) and held there—this is a new base price, not a short-term price spike. \nBangladesh, which buys 49.22 per cent of India’s yarn exports, is running its mills at roughly half capacity because the country’s gas company (Petrobangla) lost 40 of its 115 LNG shipments.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/bangladesh-gas-crisis-drives-orders-to-ludhiana-310225-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-11-006", "date": "2026-05-11", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 20, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "SIMA hails India’s ECLGS 5.0 support amid West Asia crisis", "content": "The Southern India Mills’ Association (SIMA) welcomed the Government of India’s ECLGS 5.0 scheme, calling it a timely liquidity support measure for the textile industry amid the ongoing West Asia crisis.\nThe scheme offers collateral-free loans, extended repayment tenure, and enhanced credit support to help textile firms manage rising raw material costs, logistics disruptions, and financial stress.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/sima-hails-india-s-eclgs-5-0-support-amid-west-asia-crisis-310226-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-11-007", "date": "2026-05-11", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 20, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "UK–India CETA’s 12-point tariff cut reshapes apparel sourcing", "content": "UK-India CETA removes up to 12 per cent UK duty on Indian apparel across 1,143 tariff lines, giving India parity with Bangladesh. \nUK textile imports from India reached $1.95 billion in 2025, with annual duty savings of about $156 million. \nAEPC expects Indian RMG exports to the UK to rise from $1.45 billion to $3.25 billion. \nSS27 will be the first season fully priced under CETA. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/uk-india-ceta-s-12-point-tariff-cut-reshapes-apparel-sourcing-310223-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
